    <GaugingStation location="Lanelay" name="Ely" number="57010">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station with standard Flat V weir. Flows affected by effluent returns and industrial/agricultural abstractions.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Non-standard Flat V weir installed in May 1974 to stabilise bed. New flat V weir installed 1999 resulting in new rating being applied. Fish baffles installed on downstream side of weir in 2000. Multiple peak flow ratings applied across period of record. Most recent rating validated by gaugings up to 1.8m.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station with standard Flat V weir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Flows from 16/10/2010 to 3/11/2010 suspect due to blocking of the inlet pipe. Peak flows from 01/10/1973 to 30/09/1999 rejected because of uncertainty in rating curves due to lack of gaugings in the upper limb. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). Ratings reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed for full period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Flows affected by effluent returns and industrial/agricultural abstractions.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Coal Measures. Ely valley generally steep sided. Some forest. Soils have permeable substrate. Lowland catchment. Dairy and livestock farming with urban and industrial development in the valley.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
